Review: Percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy versus nasogastric tube feeding for adults with swallowing disturbances
Total studies to screen: 66

SELECTION CRITERIA:
We planned to include randomised controlled trials comparing PEG versus NGT for adults with swallowing disturbances or 
dysphagia and indications for nutritional support, with any underlying diseases. The primary outcome was intervention 
failure (e.g. feeding interruption, blocking or leakage of the tube, no adherence to treatment).

INSTRUCTIONS: For each study below, decide INCLUDE or EXCLUDE.
Return exactly one decision object per study; do not omit excluded studies, do not summarize exclusions in bulk, and do 
not return only included studies.
