  personalised letter explaining the purpose of the study and a reply paid envelope. We asked subjects to complete the  
  questionnaire without help if possible, and, if they could not, to give it to a relative or carer willing to respond  
  for them. A reminder letter and questionnaire were sent after two weeks. The primary measures of outcome for each     
  instrument were: the frequency of response after the first mailing and the reminder and the number of forms with "no  
  domains of missing data." The study was powered (power= 0.95=(1-ß), α= 0.05) to detect an absolute difference in      
  overall response of 5%—that is, of 50 forms per 1000 between the two groups, assuming an overall mean response of     
  75%.bmj.com"}, {"study_index": 8, "title": "Relationships between oral health, dysphagia and undernutrition in        
  hospitalised elderly patients", "abstract": "Objective The aim of this study was to describe relationships between    
  oral status, dysphagia and malnutrition in a hospitalised older people.   Background Undernutrition in older people   
  is a major concern in geriatric hospital wards. Different factors can modify nutritional status like dysphagia or     
